# Phoenix OS — Flatpak Support Package List
# File: live-build/package-lists/070-flatpak.list.chroot
#
# Flatpak runtime packages. The Flathub repository is configured
# via the hook: live-build/hooks/live/0900-setup-flatpak.hook.chroot
# Actual Flatpak apps are NOT pre-installed in the ISO to keep image size
# manageable. Users install them post-boot via Discover or flatpak CLI.

# ============================================================
# Flatpak runtime
# ============================================================
flatpak                     # Flatpak application sandboxing runtime
flatpak-xdg-utils           # XDG portal utilities for Flatpak
xdg-desktop-portal          # Portal framework (required by Flatpak on Wayland)
xdg-desktop-portal-kde      # KDE implementation of XDG desktop portals
xdg-utils                   # XDG utilities (xdg-open, xdg-mime, etc.)

# ============================================================
# KDE Discover (Flatpak GUI frontend)
# ============================================================
plasma-discover             # KDE software center
plasma-discover-backend-flatpak  # Flatpak backend for Discover

# ============================================================
# AppImage support (bonus format support for creator tools)
# ============================================================
libfuse2                    # FUSE2 (required by most AppImages)
fuse3                       # FUSE3 (for newer AppImages)

# ============================================================
# Notes on Flatpak app recommendations
# ============================================================
# The following Flatpak apps are recommended for installation post-boot
# and are documented in Phoenix Welcome. They are NOT pre-installed.
#
# Creative tools:
#   org.gimp.GIMP                    - Image editing
#   org.inkscape.Inkscape            - Vector graphics
#   org.blender.Blender              - 3D creation suite
#   org.kde.kdenlive                 - Video editing
#   org.audacityteam.Audacity        - Audio editing
#   org.libreoffice.LibreOffice      - Office suite
#
# Repair and developer tools:
#   io.balena.etcher                 - USB image writer (Balena Etcher)
#   com.github.Eloston.UngoogledChromium - Browser for research
#   org.wireshark.Wireshark          - Packet analysis (GUI)
#
# Phoenix OS custom apps (installed as .deb, not Flatpak):
#   phoenix-control-center           - Installed via phoenix-control-center.deb
#   phoenix-recovery                 - Installed via phoenix-recovery.deb
